{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-132522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration in the double integral ${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{{x}^{2}+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/a65b8ea83edc85a0b0ec3f3df6ee6f5bc841e9cb5d634aab963054f836965146.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+1\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{y-1},\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=2.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 5,\\,\\sqrt{y-1}\\le x\\le 2},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/d10ba1db82f9d0366edb446f8bef564030fea2068066c7f05f388f0c9daa3414.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{{x}^{2}+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y-1}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-132522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y+1}}^{4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y-1}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{2}^{\\sqrt{y-1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y+1}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y-1}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y-1}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/def6c95bc51de3e02b913d9951cce283285cd8049375c6842719c46d33a29a15.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,⟹\\,x={e}^{y}\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=e.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,{e}^{y}\\le x\\le e},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/e38a26dbfaa0c126ec31b44f2a7d31225666779bea7b6f8b67dc2cd04e703114.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{y}}^{e}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-82200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{y}}^{e}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{e}{\\int }_{{e}^{y}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{y}}{\\int }_{1}^{e}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{y}}^{e}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/8287ba53b227ddc36aff486ea8d42a83203940ee265163320c19ad6cdb39089e.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{y}\n$$\n\nand the left boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/2c9a41f06d7edfbad9756923d9b70f1d0ffd730350d0b7d2d0e109c1bca9f80d.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-82210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration in the double integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{{e}^{y}}^{5}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/7e0a0b1860f316f7954e85b9d7f6567d9e0c05bf316cb8af3901037abe6fd17e.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡5,\\,{e}^{y}\\le x\\le 5}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx={e}^{y}\\,⟹\\,y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 5,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/3c95dd90ad02ab708f5893e47e7d7d0c8a212c18aed1972fb1bba1362181c383.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{{e}^{y}}^{5}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-132526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{e}^{4}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82196" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration in the double integral ${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2y-2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82196" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/062d32beb0cab13297c21b2eab703fd5e598191c96daa93a9c27337af95a1930.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,2y-2\\le x\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=2y-2\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{x+2}{2},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=1.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le \\frac{x+2}{2}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/543ffc57d0d32ae9a4bdefa87bd56deb7380061004b7737cf821117b4fb20e2f.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2y-2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{(x+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82196" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-82196" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82196" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{(x+2)/2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{(x+2)/2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2}^{(x+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{(x+2)/2}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{(x+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82196" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{(x+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-38601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "By changing the order of integration in the following double integrals, express the following sum as a single double integral.\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-38601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/ea36f1ec1ddeb03dd8d133fb8d65b5d50b3fa07ba34495978d87f95742dee042.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It consists of two type I regions, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le x}\\,\\cup \\,{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny=x\\,⟹\\,x=y\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=4-x\\,⟹\\,x=4-y.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,y\\le x\\le 4-y},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/e82098a4bb63f1d709a06b6a24da078594716d6a3cc0fa2e069af9dcd9154955.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{4-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-38601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-38601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-38601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{4-y}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{4-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{4-y}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{y}^{4-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{y}^{4-y}{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-38601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{4-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-1}^{1-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/e6b8889f9e8025cfca1ee0ae61b67a2f7ec9ec4aee15fab78d2f418a655bbcb8.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,{y}^{2}-1\\le x\\le 1-y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type I regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/52640b30ded8bf2cd19fe7860c7640bde3c8427ae8978f32fb8020b2f7215468.png)\n\nNotice that the bottom and top boundaries of the left region, written in the form $y=y(x),$  are \n\n$\\,$ $y=0\\,$ and $\\,y=\\sqrt{x+1}.$\n\nAlso, the bottom and top boundaries of the right region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $y=0\\,$ and $\\,y=1-x.$ \n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x+1}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-1}^{1-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-132573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x-1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x-1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x-1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}/4}^{{y}^{2}/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/7212dd3ebd7ef05423c29ca6c3bd8524f8b336563d4618a960a375121c2b2157.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\le x\\le \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type I regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/3eedf80b599bfaa97ad5cb42178359e24048938637f60a93e7ebb15cd8d8d2e4.png)\n\nNotice that the bottom and top boundaries of the left region, written in the form $y=y(x),$  are \n\n$\\,$ $y=2\\sqrt{-x}\\,$ and $\\,y=2.$\n\nAlso, the bottom and top boundaries of the right region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $y=2\\sqrt{x}\\,$ and $\\,y=2.$ \n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,2\\sqrt{-x}\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2\\sqrt{x}\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}/4}^{{y}^{2}/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{-x}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-132577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-2\\sqrt{x}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{-x}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-2\\sqrt{x}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{-x}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{-x}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-2\\sqrt{x}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{-x}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{-x}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "By changing the order of integration in the following double integrals, express the following sum as a single double integral.\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1-e}^{0}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-y)}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{e-1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/3426e7bdd134bc9af5a3665f8c9c55a65514afa9dca5be112eabb37479c4c9ec.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It consists of two type II regions, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,1-e\\le y\\le 0,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-y)\\le x\\le 1}\\,\\cup \\,{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le e-1,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)\\le x\\le 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)\\,⟹\\,y={e}^{x}-1,\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-y)\\,⟹\\,y=1-{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1-{e}^{x}\\le y\\le {e}^{x}-1},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/7d88d351b481859ec3e77350d3679387836d2e7f67325caca50e2f61cce9dcce.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1-e}^{0}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-y)}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{e-1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-{e}^{x}}^{{e}^{x}-1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-132565" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132565" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{1-{e}^{x}}^{{e}^{x}-1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-1-{e}^{x}}^{{e}^{x}+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1-{e}^{x}}^{{e}^{x}-1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1-{e}^{x}}^{{e}^{x}+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-{e}^{x}}^{{e}^{x}-1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132565" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-{e}^{x}}^{{e}^{x}-1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x-1}^{\\sqrt{1-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/0e338b779e846bc3f5ac981c93f9cda65b63d654c1152aa423f855d12d7978d9.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,x-1\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-x}}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type II regions. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/d2d1df8652af81fbcb789ac05a2d1bf43f9b5b12f394159d0eb17b4ecec90042.png)\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the lower region, written in the form $x=x(y),$  is \n\n$\\,$ $x=y+1.$\n\nAlso, the right boundary of the upper region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$\\,$ $x=1-{y}^{2}.$\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,0\\le x\\le y+1}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le 1-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x-1}^{\\sqrt{1-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{y+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-82255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{y+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{y+1}^{1-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{y+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{y+1}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{1-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{y+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/fb111bd5365ad339dcddbf5e3d98b5e53cfc029ed88c3785154194f1e64d3297.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\nx=0,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. Its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/0bed4692a7a6851ef2b66cb3842ebac6b2ef7ef4ff30bed41e84b7cb71c4f5c0.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{3})[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{3})}{4}[{x}^{4}]_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{3})]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-82292" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82292" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{9}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1))"] ["math" "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{12}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1))"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{12}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82292" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{12}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1))"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{x+2}{e}^{2y-{y}^{2}/2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/3d51eade27c19494ac30ffdaf5baf8d30ffc9d18dcc3e1186cbc59412fe000c7.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,0\\le y\\le x+2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny=x+2\\,⟹\\,x=y-2,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,y-2\\le x\\le 0},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/39072bd4c2d4bd763186f4d86921eaacb990df1e862f1c60b1f764ccff422e98.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{x+2}{e}^{2y-{y}^{2}/2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-2}^{0}{e}^{2y-{y}^{2}/2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{2y-{y}^{2}/2}[{\\int }_{y-2}^{0}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{2y-{y}^{2}/2}\\cdot x\\,{|}_{y-2}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(2-y){e}^{2y-{y}^{2}/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={e}^{2y-{y}^{2}/2}\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2(2)-{2}^{2}/2}-{e}^{2(0)-{0}^{2}/2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-132640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{2}-1"] ["math" "3{e}^{2}-4"] ["math" "{e}^{2}+2"] ["math" "{e}^{2}+4"] ["math" "{e}^{2}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{2}-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132638" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{x}^{2}}4x{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132638" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/262e1b0c4e0ddf338c527b487fcadc85baac12712f91cb4c54b771e49add25b9.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\nx=0,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=4-{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{4-y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-y}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/48c874b069b55599f76a8fe1aa50c5f4db36ff8943d264a107452668d689174b.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{x}^{2}}4x{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-y}}4x{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-y}}4x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\cdot 2{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}2(4-y){e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & ={e}^{8(4)-{4}^{2}}-{e}^{8(0)-{0}^{2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{16}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132638" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-132638" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132638" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-{e}^{8}"] ["math" "{e}^{16}-1"] ["math" "{e}^{4}+1"] ["math" "{e}^{4}-{e}^{-16}"] ["math" "{e}^{8}-{e}^{-2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132638" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{16}-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral \n${\\int }_{-4}^{-1}{\\int }_{-x-3}^{1}6x{e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/bb17a906727b436562060f84cb1acae42944587cdec6311627e30163485a72d9.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-4\\le x\\le -1,\\,-x-3\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny=-x-3\\,⟹\\,x=-y-3,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=-1.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 1,\\,-y-3\\le x\\le -1},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/f80d088bb764b5dd6aa1c6d26ebd7a5b2a3894c072d81966dec4975fc0e08e59.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}{\\int }_{-x-3}^{1}6x{e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{-y-3}^{-1}6x{e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}[{\\int }_{-y-3}^{-1}6x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{-y-3}^{-1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}3((-1)^{2}-(-y-3)^{2}){e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}3(1-(y+3)^{2}){e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={e}^{3y-(y+3)^{3}}\\,{|}_{-2}^{1} \\\\  & ={e}^{3(1)-(1+3)^{3}}-{e}^{3(-2)-(-2+3)^{3}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-61}-{e}^{-7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-132644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{-15}-1"] ["math" "{e}^{-35}-1"] ["math" "{e}^{-37}-{e}^{-8}"] ["math" "{e}^{-45}-{e}^{-3}"] ["math" "{e}^{-61}-{e}^{-7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-132644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{-61}-{e}^{-7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{8}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/d5d777577f85cd577ce35bfd3a99c1e2218622d1856f4fe7ee4afe1cfd2c9f86.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 8,\\,\\sqrt[3]{y}\\le x\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt[3]{y}\\,⟹\\,y={x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. Its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/05ec37a8f4fd33c05a2438df5c5fbc697f8b560fde0b9fe73922a0db56a09c2c.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}[{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}[y]_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{{x}^{4}}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{16}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d921303ed21a4d2633e29ee71f25a098d256b2f00d96530e543c7466d40707e5"} {"question" "q-82296" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82296" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-{e}^{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}(1-{e}^{16})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{16}-1)"] ["math" "{e}^{16}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "q-82296" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{16}-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/state.json" "file_sha256" "538cb50d904fb175aee8541d586ef5b6fc0276b810dff93664133b164694daa1"} {"question" "e-7196" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n$\\displaystyle \\int_0^1 \\int_{y^3}^{1} f(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}x \\: \\textrm{d}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/example-7196.json" "file_sha256" "6d217710ce47cd460e3e4db674b13170c60692a5acb329ae55e036eb1287c048"} {"question" "e-7196" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/47b8a129674d4644593741607e0efd5dea1ffde45357f327e3af4e08d0bf423d.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD= \\big\\{ (x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq1, \\quad y^3 \\leq x \\leq 1 \\big\\},\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx = y^3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\sqrt[3]{x},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny = 0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD= \\big\\{ (x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\quad 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt[3]{x} \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/e627a8750d3f5055b3936d47100fc51ae68926dfdc0c53d020638c9ef99f9b27.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/example-7196.json" "file_sha256" "6d217710ce47cd460e3e4db674b13170c60692a5acb329ae55e036eb1287c048"} {"question" "e-7195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration in the double integral $\\displaystyle \\int_0^1\\int_{2x}^{3-x} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm{d}y\\,\\textrm{d}x .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/example-7195.json" "file_sha256" "1c28315dc7933411f8922805232c144f3438cf5a97f6f13618d220528de0b2b2"} {"question" "e-7195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/47f6b583b2dd059ad8df49b0ca4374a964b4a28e91eb242a0dd3c7b8476fd26e.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\big\\{ (x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\quad 2x \\leq y \\leq 3-x \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type II regions. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/35b4b57f26c7903189899ec284faa39bb70fb3a80397b772376358d4d86b3ec1.png)\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the lower region, written in the form $x=x(y),$  is \n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{y}{2}.\n$$\n\nAlso, the right boundary of the upper region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=3-y.\n$$\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\Big\\{ (x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{y}{2} \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nD_2 = \\Big\\{ (x,y) \\::\\: 2 \\leq y \\leq 3, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq 3-y \\Big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2x}^{3-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/example-7195.json" "file_sha256" "1c28315dc7933411f8922805232c144f3438cf5a97f6f13618d220528de0b2b2"} {"question" "e-7194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^{1} \\int_{\\sqrt{x}}^{1 } 9\\sqrt{y^3+1}\\,\\textrm{d}y\\,\\textrm{d}x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/example-7194.json" "file_sha256" "3abf4b1e80ecf612742bae17c516e41e3efd27a3869216b1684563565aa557f5"} {"question" "e-7194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/1045aaad8025b20309b92477b4a1cf98e138064210c6fbc960c64ec26c9951df.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\quad \\sqrt{x} \\leq y \\leq 1 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\nx=0,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny = \\sqrt{x} \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx=y^2.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as type II region. Its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq y^2 \\big\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/assets/40cbaaff270daddf4b60115cc272fbc8b165b83b8823d19de2c19802617ebdb4.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{1}9\\sqrt{{y}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}9\\sqrt{{y}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{y}^{3}+1}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{y}^{3}+1}[x\\,]_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dy \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{y}^{2}({y}^{3}+1)^{1/2}\\,dy \\\\  & =3{[\\frac{2}{3}({y}^{3}+1)^{3/2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[2({y}^{3}+1)^{3/2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2(2)^{3/2}-2 \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071085/example-7194.json" "file_sha256" "3abf4b1e80ecf612742bae17c516e41e3efd27a3869216b1684563565aa557f5"}] "usage" {"e-7195" [] "e-7196" [] "e-7194" [] "q-38601" []} "basis" 2527 "retractions" [[17592186129613 :question/problem "By changing the order of integration in the following double integrals, express the following sum as a single double integral.\n\n$∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}f(x, y)dydx + ∫_{2}^{4}∫_{0}^{4 - x}f(x, y)dydx$"] [17592186128945 :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral\n$\\displaystyle \\int_0^1 \\int_{y^3}^{1} f(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}x \\: \\textrm{d}y$."] [17592186128945 :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1997/Source/Images/25d522dde8ecc0a0a3957dae03108ac8.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD= \\big\\{(x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq1, \\quad y^3 \\leq x \\leq 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y)$, is\n\n$$\nx = y^3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\sqrt[3]{x}\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny = 0\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD= \\big\\{(x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\quad 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt[3]{x} \\big\\}\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1997/Source/Images/925312e310acb44953022570595a9942.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1}∫_{y^{3}}^{1}f(x, y)dxdy &= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{x}}f(x, y)dydx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128944 :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral $\\displaystyle \\int_0^1\\int_{2x}^{3-x} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm{d}y\\,\\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186128944 :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1997/Source/Images/d5f8a21d03c9e61e36a15cd45faecbfa.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\big\\{(x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\quad 2x \\leq y \\leq 3-x \\big\\}\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type II regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1997/Source/Images/4e6985e72db38bb32ef0c05926b8ba59.png)\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the lower region, written in the form $x=x(y)$, is\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{y}{2}\n$$\n\nAlso, the right boundary of the upper region, written in the form $x=x(y)$, is\n$x=3-y$.\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\Big\\{(x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{y}{2} \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nD_2 = \\Big\\{(x,y) \\::\\: 2 \\leq y \\leq 3, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq 3-y \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1}∫_{2x}^{3 - x}f(x, y)dydx &= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{y/2}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{2}^{3}∫_{0}^{3 - y}f(x, y)dxdy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128943 :question/problem "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^{1} \\int_{\\sqrt{x}}^{1} 9\\sqrt{y^3+1}\\,\\textrm{d}y\\,\\textrm{d}x}$."] [17592186128943 :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1997/Source/Images/b061a691651d115b218622521988a608.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{(x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\quad \\sqrt{x} \\leq y \\leq 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x)$, is\n\n$$\nx=0\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x)$, is\n\n$$\ny = \\sqrt{x} \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x=y^2\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as type II region. Its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{(x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq y^2 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1997/Source/Images/a2cd4b5f56b6c6f034e5205b72232a90.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1}∫_{\\sqrt{x}}^{1}9\\sqrt{y^{3} + 1}dydx &= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{y^{2}}9\\sqrt{y^{3} + 1}dxdy \\\\\n&= 9∫_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{y^{3} + 1}[∫_{0}^{y^{2}}dx]dy \\\\\n&= 9∫_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{y^{3} + 1}[x]_{0}^{y^{2}}dy \\\\\n&= 3∫_{0}^{1}3y^{2}(y^{3} + 1)^{1/2}dy \\\\\n&= 3[\\frac{2}{3}(y^{3} + 1)^{3/2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= [2(y^{3} + 1)^{3/2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= 2(2)^{3/2} - 2 \\\\\n&= 4\\sqrt{2} - 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186127473 17592186127474 17592186127475 17592186127476 17592186127477] "immutable_fields" [[17592186127472 :answer-field/correct] [17592186127472 :answer-field/id] [17592186127472 :answer-field/key